==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|aboundant|abundaunt|habundaunt|habundant||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
First attested about 1380. From {{inh|en|enm|abundaunt}},<ref name=AHD>{{R:American Heritage Dictionary|edition=1971|page=6}}</ref> {{m|enm|habundaunt}},<ref name=WI3>{{R:MW3 1976|page=8}}</ref> {{m|enm|aboundant}}, from {{der|en|xno|abundant}}, from {{der|en|fro|abondant}}, from {{der|en|la|abundāns}}, present participle of {{m|la|abundo||to overflow, to abound}}. Compare {{m|en|abound}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/əˈbʌn.dənt/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/əˈbʌn.dənt/|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-abundant.ogg|a=US}}
* {{hyph|en|a|bun|dant}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Fully sufficient; found in [[copious]] supply; in great quantity; overflowing. {{defdate|First attested around 1350 to 1470.}}<ref name=SOED>{{R:SOED5|page=10}}</ref>
#: {{ant|en|rare|scarce}}
#: {{ux|en|Blackberries are '''abundant''' in this part of the country in October, so we always make lots of jam.}}
#: {{ux|en|an '''abundant''' selection of carpets to choose from}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=a. 1859|author=w:Leigh Hunt|title=On the Realities of Imagination
|passage=[W]ith their magical words they [poets] bring forth to our eyesight the '''abundant''' images and beauties of creation.}}
#* {{quote-video game|en|developer=w:BioWare|title={{w|Mass Effect: Andromeda}}|genre=[[science fiction|Science Fiction]]|location=Redwood City|publisher=Electronic Arts|year=2017|system=PC|scene=Kadara|oclc=1261299044|text=Kadara was of great interest to the Andromeda Initiative after it appeared on long-range surveys. Seemingly '''abundant''' liquid water and an oxygen-mix atmosphere made it a strong candidate for settlement, earning it the designation Habitat 4. Closer range surveys now reveal that Kadara's water sources are tainted and unpotable.}}
# Richly [[supplied]]; [[wealthy]]; possessing in great quantity. {{defdate|First attested around 1350 to 1470.}}<ref name=SOED/>
#* {{RQ:KJV|Exodus|34|6|passage='''Abundant''' in goodness and truth.}}
# {{lb|en|mathematics}} Being an [[abundant number]], i.e. less than the sum of all of its [[divisor]]s except itself. {{defdate|First attested in the mid 16<sup>th</sup> century.}}<ref name=SOED/>
#: {{ant|en|deficient}}

====Usage notes====
* {{sense|richly supplied}} Normally followed by the word '''in''' or {{qualifier|obsolete}} '''of'''.

